<title>GERMANY: VW says expects early good new Golf sales.</title>
<headline>VW says expects early good new Golf sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG expects to sell a good 700,000 of its new Golf vehicles in the first year, VW chief executive Ferdinand Piech said on Monday.</p>
<p>Piech made the comment in an interview with German television network n-tv ahead of the world premiere of the new version of the popular vehicle on Tuesday in Bonn.</p>
<p>VW, which is based in Wolfsburg, sold about 700,000 of the popular Golf models in 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
